<%# One student's row.

    **Inputs are sized to their content.** They were `w-full`, which is right for a form column and
    wrong in a table cell: the days input rendered at **322px** for a value that cannot exceed two
    digits, because the column took the table's slack. GOV.UK states the rule and ships width-2/3/4/5
    modifiers for exactly this - so days is w-20 (80px, two or three digits plus Chrome's spinner) and a
    grade is w-24 (96px, two characters plus the chevron's 36px). The utility beats `tw-input-primary`'s
    `w-full` deliberately here, which is the one place that override is wanted.

    **Perfect attendance is a segmented Yes/No, not a checkbox.** A bare tick said nothing about what
    was being answered; GOV.UK reserves a single checkbox for opting in and gives a yes/no question
    radios. `.tw-segmented` is two native radios, so the keyboard behaviour is the browser's.

    **Every control names itself**, including the student, because a row is identified visually only. A
    `<th>` names a data cell, never a form control.

    display_name, not username: it prefers the student's name and falls back to the username. Nothing
    changes today because no student has a name - the add-student form collects only a username, which
    is in design-todo - but the lowercase identifiers on screen are usernames, and capitalising them
    would be wrong. %>
<% who = entry.user.display_name %>
<% unattended_bonus = entry.is_perfect_attendance && entry.attendance_days.to_i.zero? %>

<tr id="<%= dom_id(entry) %>" class="table-body-row">
  <%= fields_for "grade_entries[]", entry do |f| %>
    <td class="table-body-cell whitespace-nowrap">
      <% if entry.username.present? %>
        <span class="font-medium text-slate-900"><%= who %></span>
      <% else %>
        <span class="text-slate-600 italic">No username set</span>
      <% end %>
    </td>

    <td class="table-body-cell whitespace-nowrap">
      <%= f.select :math_grade,
                   options_for_select(GradeEntry::GRADE_OPTIONS, entry.math_grade),
                   { include_blank: true },
                   disabled:,
                   class: "tw-input-primary w-24",
                   aria: { label: "Math grade for #{who}" },
                   data: { testid: "math-grade-select" } %>
    </td>

    <td class="table-body-cell whitespace-nowrap">
      <%= f.select :reading_grade,
                   options_for_select(GradeEntry::GRADE_OPTIONS, entry.reading_grade),
                   { include_blank: true },
                   disabled:,
                   class: "tw-input-primary w-24",
                   aria: { label: "Reading grade for #{who}" },
                   data: { testid: "reading-grade-select" } %>
    </td>

    <td class="table-body-cell whitespace-nowrap">
      <%= f.number_field :attendance_days,
                         class: "tw-input-primary w-20",
                         disabled:,
                         min: 0,
                         aria: { label: "Days attended by #{who}" },
                         data: { testid: "attendance-days-input" } %>

      <%# The inline half of the warning, under the field it is about - the summary above the table is
          the other half, which is this app's own form-error shape. Amber, not `tw-field-error`: that
          token is red, and a bonus with no days recorded is a warning to check rather than a failure. %>
      <% if unattended_bonus %>
        <span class="mt-1 block text-xs font-medium text-amber-700" data-testid="unattended-bonus">
          No days recorded
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </td>

    <td class="table-body-cell whitespace-nowrap">
      <span class="tw-segmented" data-testid="perfect-attendance-control">
        <% { true => "Yes", false => "No" }.each do |value, label| %>
          <%= f.radio_button :is_perfect_attendance, value,
                             class: "sr-only",
                             disabled:,
                             aria: { label: "Perfect attendance bonus for #{who}: #{label}" } %>
          <%= f.label :is_perfect_attendance, label,
                      value: value,
                      class: "tw-segmented-option" %>
        <% end %>
      </span>
    </td>

    <%= render "entry_earnings", entry: entry, earnings: grade_book_earnings %>
  <% end %>
</tr>
